interface.longDescription:
Fleek is an app for keeping track of the subscriptions you pay for. Fleek Tracker connects your own Fleek account to ChatGPT, so you can ask about your subscriptions in plain language.

It can:
- list the subscriptions you track in Fleek, with each one's plan, cost, renewal or end date and whether autopay is on, soonest renewal first;
- give your monthly total in one currency, saying how many plans in other currencies it left out;
- show subscriptions that have ended, if you ask;
- add subscriptions you name or confirm, for example from a bill or a screenshot you share, if you allowed adding when you connected;
- if you ask, find your subscriptions in your email: with your email connected in ChatGPT, it tells ChatGPT where receipts usually come from in your country, ChatGPT searches your email, shows you what it found, and adds only what you confirm. Fleek never reads your email; it keeps only which company each confirmed subscription came from.

You sign in to your Fleek account once and choose whether ChatGPT may add subscriptions. You can disconnect at any time in ChatGPT.

Limitations: it cannot buy, cancel, remove or edit a subscription, and it never estimates a price or a date. It only sees what is tracked in your Fleek account.
